# Build context hygiene. node_modules is the big one: the image installs its
# own from the lockfile, and shipping the host's would both bloat the context
# and risk platform-specific binaries leaking in.
node_modules
**/node_modules
dist
**/dist

.git
.gitignore

# Secrets never enter an image layer. They arrive at run time, through
# docker-compose's env_file.
#
# The `**/` is the whole point. A pattern without it is anchored at the context
# root, so a bare `.env` excluded the root file and silently let `COPY apps/api`
# carry `apps/api/.env` — CONNECTION_SECRET and every model key — into the
# image at /app/apps/api/.env. It was mode 600 root:root there and the API runs
# as uid 1000, so nothing read it and nothing complained; what found it was a
# stdio MCP server inheriting the API's working directory and dying on the
# unreadable file. See `stdioCwd` in services/mcp/client.ts.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Local state, not application code.
apps/api/data
apps/api/workspace
workspaces
docs
pic
*.md
!README.md
